From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Sun, 30 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: keep the response cursor and the continuous-effect
 marker right for more than two duelists

Three sites change. All three are new code paths for n_duelists > 2 or give the same value at n == 2.

next_responder (field.cpp): when the cursor duelist was eliminated while its window was open, it was not in
the response order, so the result was DUELIST_NONE and the window closed before the living duelists answered.
The search for the cursor now uses the full seat order (eliminated duelists keep their place) and then takes the
next living duelist who has not passed. response_order() is unchanged for its callers: it shares one static
helper with a living_only flag. next_responder is not called at n == 2.

PhaseEvent pass (processor.cpp, step 2): the pass of an eliminated cursor no longer counts against the living
duelists, so the window cannot close one duelist early. The count is unchanged when the cursor is alive. n == 2
uses the stock priority_passed branch above it.

Continuous effects (processor.cpp, SolveContinuous case 4 and SolveChain case 8): conti_player = opponent_of(tp)
was 255 (none_id) for tp 2 and 254 (all_id) for tp 3. For tp 2 case 4 then reset the marker to the turn player,
so new turn player effects ran before the other duelists had finished. At n > 2 a separate marker value
(DUELIST_ALL - 1, local to processor.cpp) is used. At n == 2 it is still opponent_of(tp). No header change.

Not changed: next_trigger_player has the same dead cursor case (SEGOC), and a duelist who passed and was
eliminated later is still counted in PhaseEvent pass_count. Both belong to other sites.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
